<title>UK: De Beers signs mining deal with Guinea.</title>
<headline>De Beers signs mining deal with Guinea.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-07-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>South African diamond giant De Beers Consolidated Mines Ltd said on Wednesday it had signed a mining agreement with the government of Guinea to operate in that country.</p>
<p>The agreement set out guidelines under which Guinea's ministry for resources and energy and De Beers would co-operate on prospecting in the African nation.</p>
<p>The agreement also details terms for De Beers to operate discovered mines and subsequent marketing of diamonds.</p>
<p>De Beers had been involved in prospecting for kimberlites -- diamond-containing rocks -- in eastern Guinea since it bought offices for buying rough diamonds in the country in 1992.</p>
